{
  "_readme": [
    "OpenTactileCAD sensor manifest. Lengths in mm.",
    "Coordinates are Y-UP and share one frame (cable edge horizontal at the bottom), so 'outline', 'edge_cuts' and 'pixels' overlay directly. The KiCad export negates Y.",
    "'edge_cuts' is the board that gets MANUFACTURED (grown board + cable tail + connector envelope). 'outline' is only the shape the user drew - smaller, and not the cut boundary.",
    "'pixels' is [x, y, row_index, col_index] per active taxel and is the authority on where taxels physically sit.",
    "'ox'/'oy'/'px'/'py'/'m'/'rp'/'cp' are for MCU scan order, NOT geometry: their row index is pad order, which is deliberately not geometric order, so 'py' can be negative and ox+ci*px does not reproduce positions. Use 'pixels' for geometry.",
    "'w'/'h' are one taxel's footprint size; 'footprint' holds the rest of the parameters needed to redraw its interdigitated copper.",
    "'shear' says which taxels share a shear bump. 'shear.bumps' are bump centres in the same frame as 'pixels'; 'shear.b' is parallel to 'pixels' and gives each taxel's bump index, or -1 for a taxel with no bump above it (pressure only, no shear). Shear direction is the differential across the taxels of one group, signed by (pixel - bump centre); a group of fewer than 4 is a block the outline cut short and is degenerate on any axis with taxels on one side only. The bump SHEET is optional and its height/taper are chosen when it is built, so they are not here - this is only where bumps would go. Added retroactively to this already-fabricated board; nothing else in the file was changed."
  ],
